  "definition_ja": "曲線のある区間の長さ。y = f(x) なら ∫ₐᵇ √(1 + {f′(x)}²) dx で求まる。",
  "definition_en": "The length of a curve over an interval; for y = f(x) it is ∫ₐᵇ √(1 + (f′(x))²) dx.",
  "latex": "L = \\int_a^b \\sqrt{1 + \\bigl(f'(x)\\bigr)^2}\\,dx",
  "spoken_en": "L equals the integral from a to b of the square root of one plus f prime of x squared, dx",
  "examples": [
    {
      "en": "Arc length integrals almost never come out nice unless the problem was built for it.",
      "ja": "曲線の長さの積分は、きれいに解けるように作られた問題でない限り、まずきれいな形にならない。",
      "register": "spoken"
